<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Leave Policy</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: Arial; margin: 0; background: #f4f6f8; }
    header { background: #2c3e50; color: white; padding: 15px 30px; }
    nav { background: #34495e; padding: 10px 30px; }
    nav a { color: white; margin-right: 15px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 14px; }
    .container { max-width: 900px; margin: 30px auto; padding: 20px; background: white; border-radius: 8px; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 20px; }
    th, td { padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; text-align: left; }
    th { background: #ecf0f1; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header><h1>🚜 Nourish Farm Management</h1></header>
  <nav>
    <a href="/">Home</a>
    <a href="/leave/dashboard">Leave Dashboard</a>
    <a href="/leave/policy">Leave Policy</a>
    <a href="/leave/history">Employee Leave History</a>
    <a href="/leave/apply">Apply for Leave</a>
    <a href="/leave/applications">Leave Applications</a>
  </nav>
  <div class="container">
    <h2>📜 Company Leave Policy</h2>
    <p>Standard annual leave entitlement for all employees (subject to joining date calculations for PCL and Casual Leave):</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Leave Name</th><th>Standard Annual Balance</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Project Casual Leave</td><td>52 Days (Calculated based on joining date)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Casual Leave</td><td>10 Days (Calculated based on joining date)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Medical Leave</td><td>14 Days</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Marriage Leave</td><td>5 Days</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Paternity Leave</td><td>3 Days</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Hajj Leave</td><td>45 Days</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Omrah Leave</td><td>10 Days</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bereavement Leave</td><td>3 Days</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Earn Leave</td><td>16 Days (1 day per 18 working days, max 16/year)</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p><b>Note:</b> Only Earn Leave can be carried forward to the next year. All other leaves expire at the end of the year.</p>
  </div>
</body>
</html>